.TH CLEAR 1
.SH NAME
clear \- clear the screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clear
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clear
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It clears the terminal and puts the cursor at its top left (it writes
.BR "ESC[H ESC[J" ,
which the console, the desktop's terminals and other terminals
understand).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR con (4),
.BR sh (1)
